11. SITEMAP.XML

Generate a valid XML sitemap for the website's canonical, indexable URLs.

Example structure:

"https://pdflove.store/sitemap.xml"

Include the homepage, important informational pages and eligible individual tool pages.

Example XML template:

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://pdflove.store/</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://pdflove.store/tools/merge-pdf</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://pdflove.store/tools/compress-pdf</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://pdflove.store/tools/jpg-to-pdf</loc>
  </url>
</urlset>

The above is a template, not a complete sitemap.

Generate entries for all actual eligible tool URLs and the appropriate informational pages.

Requirements:

- Use absolute HTTPS URLs.
- Include only real, canonical URLs that should be indexed.
- Do not include login, temporary processing, blob, query-generated duplicate or error URLs.
- Use valid XML escaping.
- Use "lastmod" only when it reflects a genuine modification date.
- Do not add arbitrary "priority" or "changefreq" values as if they improve Google rankings.
- Split into sitemap indexes if the sitemap grows beyond protocol limits.
- Ensure the sitemap returns valid XML with HTTP status 200.
- Reference the sitemap in "robots.txt".
- Provide a generated sitemap file or a hosting-compatible sitemap-generation solution.

Important: A sitemap cannot be made publicly available merely by placing its XML inside an HTML script element. If hosting only allows the main HTML file, explain the platform limitation and provide a real supported alternative.

